  "inner_store_type_convention": "the specification places a one-byte inner store type at the head of the layer-2 plaintext. The oracle's encrypt helper prepends that byte itself, so its caller passes the bare LeaseSet2 record; i2pr's API takes the store type and the record separately and prepends it. The two conventions are equivalent, which is why the outer ciphertexts are byte-identical. Handing the oracle an already-prefixed record produces a layer-2 plaintext one byte longer and a correspondingly longer outer ciphertext."
